"The still one's name, stamped on the copper tag, is Aeron."
"Before the iron, Aeron's scales were storm-blue."
"A healer of the old sanctuary hid Aeron's name in her roll; the keepers drowned her for tending him."
"Aeron stopped wanting a hundred years ago, when his sister's pull went silent and he took her for dead."
"As his magic returns, Aeron will feel his sister's pull again, faint and asleep."
"Feeling his sister alive is what can wake Aeron's wanting."
